    {
      "id": "section:9/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "Common kernel fault: `copy_to_user` / `copy_from_user` with an invalid user pointer.",
      "source_hash": 15251413025265218539,
      "context_hash": 6355301068488649308,
      "translation": "흔한 커널 폴트로는 잘못된 사용자 포인터를 사용한 `copy_to_user` / `copy_from_user`가 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:03:59.430685Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:9/block:2/seg:1",
      "source": "The `fixup_exception` mechanism uses a table of `{fault_address → recovery_address}` pairs — if the fault address is in the table, execution jumps to the recovery code (returns `-EFAULT`).",
